# web888d command line. `--bitstream auto` loads the variant's bitstream
# from /usr/share/web888 (package web888-bitstream) through the FPGA
# manager before /dev/zynqsdr is opened. To try another bitstream, put it
# on the boot partition (FAT, read-only at /boot) and use
# `--bitstream /boot/<file>.bit`; this file lives on the read-only root
# until the configuration partition exists.
#
# The web UI (package web888d-ui) is served on 8073, HTTPS and plain HTTP
# on one port. Its self-signed certificate would be kept in
# /var/lib/web888d, which is read-only for now: a new one is made at each
# start, so browsers ask again after every reboot. `--tls-cert/--tls-key`
# point at a fixed pair (e.g. on /boot).
WEB888D_ARGS="serve"
